"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[7977],{97977:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"dollar-86-rubley-minfin-pokupki-valyuty","locale":"en","title":"Dollar rises above 86 rubles as Finance Ministry increases currency purchases 5-fold","description":"The dollar exceeded 86 rubles on October 6. From October 7, the Finance Ministry buys 12.7 billion rubles of currency daily. How oil prices weaken the ruble through the budget rule.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"On the morning of October 6, the dollar reached 86.1 rubles over the counter. It had not exceeded 86 since September 9. The euro rose 0.6% to 96.3 rubles and the yuan 0.7% to 12.8. The Bank of Russia calculates official rates from the previous day\'s trading, so its October 6 dollar rate was lower, at 84.93 rubles, up 1.45 from the day before. On October 1 the official rate was 83.56. Globally, the dollar instead fell on October 5, showing the ruble was weakening for domestic reasons."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"On October 5, the Finance Ministry announced purchases of currency and gold worth 279.42 billion rubles from October 7 to November 6, or 12.7 billion daily. In the preceding month it spent 2.5 billion daily. The Bank of Russia simultaneously sells 0.58 billion rubles of currency a day; after those sales, net state purchases will be 12.12 billion daily. September\'s equivalent was 1.92 billion, a 6.3-fold difference. The state has not bought this much since early 2022. Purchases start only on October 7, but markets reacted to the announcement."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Oil provided the funds. Russia\'s budget is based on Urals at $59 per barrel. When oil is dearer, tax on the difference is saved in the National Wealth Fund through currency and gold purchases rather than spent. This threshold is called the cutoff price. Oil companies pay a month in arrears: October payments cover September. August Urals was $67.11, only modestly above the threshold. September was $92.08, so October\'s expected excess revenue is 289.46 billion rubles. Purchases are 279.42 billion because the ministry deducted 10.04 billion after September revenue fell short of its estimate."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"In itself, the rule should not move the ruble. Oil companies sell more currency to pay higher taxes, and the ministry buys that currency. Timing is the problem. Starting October 7, the ministry buys equal amounts daily, while exporters sell most near month-end before tax payments. Early in the month, buyers outnumber sellers and the ruble weakens. Chinese holidays through October 7 also reduce yuan trading, allowing a large purchase to move the rate more sharply."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"Further ruble weakness would reach travel, electronics and car prices tied to currency. From October 1 to 6, the official dollar rate rose 1.6%. The Bank of Russia\'s 14% key rate supports the ruble: ruble deposits are more attractive than foreign-currency deposits. Exporters\' month-end currency sales for taxes usually help too. It is not yet possible to say how far those sales will offset ministry purchases."},{"id":"b006","kind":"paragraph","text":"Timing matters to anyone planning to exchange rubles. The rate is currently lifted by a monthly purchase programme ending on November 6. But if October oil stays expensive, November purchases will again be large because November taxes use October\'s oil price."},{"id":"b007","kind":"heading","text":"Why did the dollar rise in October 2026?"},{"id":"b008","kind":"paragraph","text":"From October 7, the ministry will buy currency and gold worth 12.7 billion rubles daily, 5 times September\'s amount. A large market buyer pushes currency prices up, and the market reacted immediately: on October 6 the dollar exceeded 86 rubles for the first time since September 9."},{"id":"b009","kind":"heading","text":"What is the budget rule\'s cutoff price?"},{"id":"b010","kind":"paragraph","text":"It is the oil price underlying the budget, $59 per barrel in 2026. Tax revenue above that level is saved in the National Wealth Fund through currency and gold purchases instead of spent."},{"id":"b011","kind":"heading","text":"How long will purchases remain at this scale?"},{"id":"b012","kind":"paragraph","text":"The current amount applies from October 7 to November 6. The ministry will announce a new amount in early November, depending on October\'s oil price."}],"sources":[{"label":"Finance Ministry to increase currency and gold purchases fivefold from October 7","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1120386"},{"label":"Finance Ministry to buy 279.42 billion rubles of currency and gold from October 7 to November 6","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9006327"},{"label":"Finance Ministry and central bank to increase October currency purchases more than 6-fold","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/10/05/update-1-minfin-i-tsbr-narastyat-pokupki-valyuty-v-oktyabre-bolee-chem-v-6-raz-do-1212-mlrd-r-v-den-a207802"},{"label":"Dollar exceeds 86 rubles for the first time since September 9","url":"https://www.kommersant.ru/doc/9007053"},{"label":"Ruble weakens against the yuan in morning trading","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1120563"},{"label":"Central bank raises official dollar rate by almost 1.5 rubles","url":"https://finance.mail.ru/article/tsb-povyisil-ofitsialnyij-kurs-dollara-pochti-na-15-69231003/"},{"label":"Official dollar rate falls below 84 rubles","url":"https://www.vedomosti.ru/finance/news/2026/09/30/1233185-kurs-opustilsya"},{"label":"New cutoff price for oil revenue","url":"https://www.fontanka.ru/2026/09/09/76634061/"},{"label":"Urals rises in September in the Baltic, India and China","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1119753"},{"label":"Stocks upbeat, dollar wobbles as Fed hike bets recede","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/stocks-upbeat-dollar-wobbles-fed-012516671.html"},{"label":"Bank of Russia keeps its key rate at 14%","url":"https://www.cbr.ru/press/keypr/"}],"sourceBodySha256":"b900eb1904932c64959784d06618a3e247429cc6ba8713c6bd8f0558bb9d2f88"}')}}]);